  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "For a finite group G, let End(G) denote the semigroup of endomorphisms\nof G, and PIso(G) the semigroup of partial isomorphisms of G (isomorphisms between\nsubgroups of G). If G is abelian, then |End(G)| = |PIso(G)|. Is the converse true?\n                                                                           P. J. Cameron",
